        See Also
        --------
        Index.size : Return the number of elements in the underlying data.

        Examples
        --------
        >>> idx = pd.Index([1, 2, 3])
        >>> idx
        Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64')
        >>> idx.empty
        False

        >>> idx_empty = pd.Index([])
        >>> idx_empty
        Index([], dtype='object')
        >>> idx_empty.empty
        True

        If we only have NaNs in our DataFrame, it is not considered empty!

        >>> idx = pd.Index([np.nan, np.nan])
